@{5b3406530132a20f8f95c128|full_name}: Have you tried it yourself? This solution is almost useless for the following reasons:
1. In these steamvr settings, you can not set a dead zone, and without this, your character will periodically move by itself, which in a minute will annoy you;
2. The speed of movement/rotation in the game is always at the maximum;
3. Both joysticks just stop working after some random time, and you can only restart the game completely to make them work again.

I used Fishbiter/WMR_vrclient solution (which have dead zone settings + maximum stability) until recently, but it stopped working after the last SteamVR update; (
